Package: azan-sip-client
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Azan SIP <noreply@github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/Fudgeamin99/azan-sip-box
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), cage, xwayland, seatd, chromium, libgl1-mesa-dri, fonts-dejavu-core, alsa-utils, dbus, libpam-systemd, iproute2, libnss-mdns
Recommends: avahi-daemon, alsa-ucm-conf
Suggests: firmware-intel-sound
Description: Azan SIP Box prayer times and azan on a TV (for a Dell Wyse)
 Turns a small Debian computer, such as a Dell Wyse thin client, into a TV
 screen for the Azan SIP Box. It shows the box's prayer-times screen full
 screen on the TV plugged into it, from every boot, and plays the azan
 through the TV's speakers at the same moment as the phones, at a volume of
 its own. It finds the box on the network, and reconnects by itself after
 the box restarts or the network drops.
